Export gfxstream resources on demand and query their layout lazily.

gfxstream gives a color buffer its final, importable layout (an explicit DRM
modifier) when the VMM first exports it for scanout, so exporting every 3D
resource at creation would freeze the wrong layout and keep an fd per
resource. Add export_blob and query to the RutabagaComponent trait, let
Rutabaga::export_blob ask the component when no handle was cached, let
Rutabaga::resource3d_info ask the component when the resource carries no 3D
info, and stop create_3d from exporting and querying eagerly. The query also
reads the offset and modifier gfxstream now reports.

